{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 2, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the last Latin count of Tripoli and the ruler of the County of Tripoli from 1187 to 1192. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Margaret of Navarre.\n\n**Early Life and Reign**\nRaymond III was born in 1150 or 1151. He succeeded his father as count of Tripoli in 1187 after the death of his father. He ruled the county for five years until he was killed in 1192 during the Third Crusade.\n\n**The Third Crusade**\nRaymond III joined the Third Crusade in 1190 with a small army of knights and men-at-arms. He landed in Acre and marched to Jaffa where he was received by King Richard I of England. However he was not well received by King Richard and was seen as a threat by the lord of the Holy Land. He was rejected by King Richard and placed under the command of the lord of the Holy Land.\n\n**Capture and Death**\nRaymond III was captured by the forces of Saladin in 1192 while on his way back from the Third Crusade. He was imprisoned in Damascus and later released in 1193. However while traveling back to his kingdom he was captured again by the Mamluk Sultan al-Adil. Raymond III and other Crusaders were taken to the Mamluk Sultan's court where he was imprisoned. He died in Damascus in 1192 due to poor conditions and lack of food and water.\n\nRaymond III was the last Latin count of Tripoli and the ruler of the County of Tripoli. He played a significant role in the Third Crusade and was a prominent figure in the Holy Land.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0011754278093576431}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001311216183239594}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.20655624568462372}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.802703940891661e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00026901919045485556}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.12716976320371e-05}, {"token": "